## Why This Is Asked

This task asks for a practical, beginner-friendly NLP feature that is directly useful in real-world chat apps: extracting and standardizing time references across languages, with on-device constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Time expression parsing across EN/ES/DE
- On-device inference with WebAssembly
- Normalization to ISO 8601 and confidence signaling

## Code Example

```javascript
function normalizeTime(text) {
  const idx = text.indexOf(":");
  if (idx > 0 && idx < text.length - 1) {
    const before = text[idx - 1];
    const after = text[idx + 1];
    if (before >= '0' && before <= '9' && after >= '0' && after <= '9') {
      const start = Math.max(0, idx - 2);
      const end = Math.min(text.length, idx + 3);
      return text.substring(start, end);
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```

